#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700570 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02e0fa51-63ce-5bc6-8479-4772fc2d2e1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700560}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02e0fa51-63ce-5bc6-8479-4772fc2d2e1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700560} :answer-field/id #uuid "18f812af-1a65-5f83-a221-1110e8ba14e3" :answer-field/key "derivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700562} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9993038-f68a-5c71-9dbf-8fff7041def9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{11}}{11}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700580}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9993038-f68a-5c71-9dbf-8fff7041def9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{11}}{11}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700580} :answer-field/id #uuid "72da51d8-78f0-5b09-ae6c-ccd24522f8d2" :answer-field/key "antiderivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700571}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "54172dfa-98f2-5433-82f3-31dd6dd5e828" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=x^{10}$ and $F'(x)=f(x)$, a student proposes\n\n$$\nG(x)=\\frac{x^{11}}{11}+C.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the proposed expression, then give the correct general antiderivative of $f$. Use $C$ for the arbitrary constant.\n\n1. $G'(x)=$ {{derivative}}.\n2. $F(x)=$ {{antiderivative}}." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the proposed expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G'(x)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{x^{11}}{11}+C\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{11}\\cdot 11x^{10}+0 \\\\ &=x^{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe proposed expression does differentiate to the given function.\n\nIntegration reverses differentiation, so $F'(x)=f(x)$ gives $F(x)=\\int f(x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nApply the power rule with $n=10$ and include an arbitrary constant $C$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x)&=\\int x^{10}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\frac{x^{10+1}}{10+1}+C \\\\ &=\\frac{x^{11}}{11}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCheck by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{x^{11}}{11}+C\\right)&=\\frac{1}{11}\\cdot 11x^{10}+0 \\\\ &=x^{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700573 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4efd4867-5512-5b91-971d-60b0f9a00d98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5 x^{4}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4efd4867-5512-5b91-971d-60b0f9a00d98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5 x^{4}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700568} :answer-field/id #uuid "e302afe6-e6bf-5a18-932e-23ba8a1299ff" :answer-field/key "derivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700581} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "486a75de-fea9-549b-abe3-43a6f3598aa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{5}}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "486a75de-fea9-549b-abe3-43a6f3598aa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{5}}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700566} :answer-field/id #uuid "f94c6270-9467-57e6-a948-c77b0fb8c8eb" :answer-field/key "antiderivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700583}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "75889302-faba-51c2-87ad-8cc85bbcab9e" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=x^{4}$ and $F'(x)=f(x)$, a student proposes\n\n$$\nG(x)=\\frac{x^{5}}{4}+C.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the proposed expression, then give the correct general antiderivative of $f$. Use $C$ for the arbitrary constant.\n\n1. $G'(x)=$ {{derivative}}.\n2. $F(x)=$ {{antiderivative}}." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the proposed expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G'(x)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{x^{5}}{4}+C\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 5x^{4}+0 \\\\ &=\\frac{5 x^{4}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe proposed expression divides by the old exponent rather than the new exponent.\n\nIntegration reverses differentiation, so $F'(x)=f(x)$ gives $F(x)=\\int f(x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nApply the power rule with $n=4$ and include an arbitrary constant $C$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x)&=\\int x^{4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\frac{x^{4+1}}{4+1}+C \\\\ &=\\frac{x^{5}}{5}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCheck by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{x^{5}}{5}+C\\right)&=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 5x^{4}+0 \\\\ &=x^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700582 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff19365c-eb62-5c2a-a0f0-f8d9ff0225bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{8}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700584}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff19365c-eb62-5c2a-a0f0-f8d9ff0225bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{8}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700584} :answer-field/id #uuid "5066c5fa-3246-598e-85b5-a3d2b0500d97" :answer-field/key "antiderivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700569} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8971dadb-c93f-5d41-9b68-b5f5ede98c4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64 x^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8971dadb-c93f-5d41-9b68-b5f5ede98c4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64 x^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700574} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0b6540a-ddd4-5e24-a329-d12b853098c4" :answer-field/key "derivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ed74f25e-aeb7-5e9d-9561-681703c592ec" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=x^{7}$ and $F'(x)=f(x)$, a student proposes\n\n$$\nG(x)=8 x^{8}+C.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the proposed expression, then give the correct general antiderivative of $f$. Use $C$ for the arbitrary constant.\n\n1. $G'(x)=$ {{derivative}}.\n2. $F(x)=$ {{antiderivative}}." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the proposed expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G'(x)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(8 x^{8}+C\\right) \\\\ &=8\\cdot 8x^{7}+0 \\\\ &=64 x^{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe proposed expression multiplies by the new exponent rather than dividing.\n\nIntegration reverses differentiation, so $F'(x)=f(x)$ gives $F(x)=\\int f(x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nApply the power rule with $n=7$ and include an arbitrary constant $C$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x)&=\\int x^{7}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\frac{x^{7+1}}{7+1}+C \\\\ &=\\frac{x^{8}}{8}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCheck by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{x^{8}}{8}+C\\right)&=\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 8x^{7}+0 \\\\ &=x^{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701883 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "061f0f90-4a8d-5b40-8c36-ad60053fb867" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\cdot 5^{2x+1}}{\\ln 5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701880} {:answer/id #uuid "121f4529-858d-5610-b420-9b3ad3f17ad3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5^{2x+1}}{\\ln 5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701881} {:answer/id #uuid "2efc5d03-1c7a-5fdc-82ff-2e0b2169a715" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5^{x+1}}{2\\ln 5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701884} {:answer/id #uuid "8c213d61-b9d7-57cb-b990-af543be51204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5^{2x+1}}{2\\ln 5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701891} {:answer/id #uuid "f23b2145-3415-5220-8b25-a5e5b55c4beb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5^{2x+1}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c213d61-b9d7-57cb-b990-af543be51204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5^{2x+1}}{2\\ln 5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701891} :answer-field/id #uuid "3808f2c1-d504-5685-9fe0-28dcbf7af8b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "23948473-1a87-519a-aebb-0dfcf24276f3" :question/problem "Calculate the integral.\n\n$$\n\\int 5^{2x+1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2x+1$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nRewrite the integral, divide by the natural logarithm of the base, and substitute back:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int 5^{2x+1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\int 5^u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=\\frac{5^u}{2\\ln 5}+C \\\\\n&=\\frac{5^{2x+1}}{2\\ln 5}+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives $\\frac{1}{2\\ln 5}\\cdot 5^{2x+1}\\ln 5\\cdot 2=5^{2x+1}$, as required."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701887 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a414560f-15e2-54c6-9305-f5ee269e72d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4\\ln 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a414560f-15e2-54c6-9305-f5ee269e72d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4\\ln 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701892} :answer-field/id #uuid "16126341-d359-5b82-a393-2ada162b391b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701882}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6151da70-5852-55b5-a17f-17bec5124984" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_0^1 3\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{1-2x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=1-2x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-2\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\mathrm{d}x=-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nThe transformed limits decrease; keep them in their corresponding order:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nThe logarithm of the reciprocal base is also negative:\n\n$$\n\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=\\ln 1-\\ln 2=-\\ln 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_0^1 3\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{1-2x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=-\\frac{3}{2}\\int_1^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=-\\frac{3}{2}\\left[\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^u}{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}\\right]_1^{-1} \\\\\n&=\\frac{3}{2\\ln 2}\\left[\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^u\\right]_1^{-1} \\\\\n&=\\frac{3}{2\\ln 2}\\left(2-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\frac{9}{4\\ln 2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe answer is positive, consistent with integrating a positive function from $0$ to $1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701889 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02845e25-f55d-5a4f-b709-604c03f454d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24}{\\ln 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701879} {:answer/id #uuid "5f46e20f-430c-505a-b1de-d0593d544a2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{\\ln 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701886} {:answer/id #uuid "67a98576-ecf7-58c9-95ba-7d885db155a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2\\ln 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701888} {:answer/id #uuid "fb0169e5-ddf8-5288-b6f7-ea98b158c4a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701894} {:answer/id #uuid "fe9aef35-2882-5952-95b0-f1ead39f6877" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{12}{\\ln 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f46e20f-430c-505a-b1de-d0593d544a2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{\\ln 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701886} :answer-field/id #uuid "836c60a3-9185-59e1-a3b3-436205db939a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8364e075-c24e-573d-8d19-c1a0a06a6ca0" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_0^1 3^{2x+1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2x+1$, so $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. Transform both limits:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n\nThen\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_0^1 3^{2x+1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\int_1^3 3^u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=\\left[\\frac{3^u}{2\\ln 3}\\right]_1^3 \\\\\n&=\\frac{3^3-3^1}{2\\ln 3} \\\\\n&=\\frac{27-3}{2\\ln 3} \\\\\n&=\\frac{12}{\\ln 3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe value is positive because the integrand is positive and the original limits increase."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701896 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d06d9d8-3b59-51d8-8b64-df3c48ff4890" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9e^{2-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701899} {:answer/id #uuid "5b5e31e9-8661-5207-920f-f50d638ffea7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-e^{2-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701900} {:answer/id #uuid "69095567-f76f-584b-9a04-f7a400196965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e^{2-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701901} {:answer/id #uuid "f0a9c3e1-4498-5c03-8a85-0d8e221fd7bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-e^{2-x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701904} {:answer/id #uuid "f195088c-2e31-5164-b9fa-1857355750bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b5e31e9-8661-5207-920f-f50d638ffea7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-e^{2-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701900} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3f54bb2-8462-5132-98aa-660c45e5acfb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701906}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "28113156-0669-5d12-8db9-eb87af8b625c" :question/problem "Calculate\n\n$$\n\\int 3e^{2-3x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2-3x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-3,\n\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=-\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nSubstitute, integrate, and replace $u$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int 3e^{2-3x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=\\int 3e^u\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=-\\int e^u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=-e^u+C \\\\\n&=-e^{2-3x}+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives $(-1)(-3)e^{2-3x}=3e^{2-3x}$, the original integrand."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701903 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dd36aa3-3c19-5941-bd8a-b4d999a0c2cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9e}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dd36aa3-3c19-5941-bd8a-b4d999a0c2cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9e}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701902} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ec792ec-9798-51e4-8eda-6d3bdebddab1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8e1b2f3d-51d9-5b7c-8030-87db307147f0" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\ln 2}^{\\ln 4}\\frac{6e^{x+1}}{e^{3x}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First use the quotient rule for exponentials to expose the linear exponent:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6e^{x+1}}{e^{3x}}=6e^{(x+1)-3x}=6e^{1-2x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=1-2x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-2,\n\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nTransform both limits, keeping them in their corresponding positions:\n\n| $x$ | $\\ln 2$ | $\\ln 4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1-2\\ln 2$ | $1-2\\ln 4$ |\n\nThe negative slope makes the upper transformed limit smaller than the lower one. Retain that order and the negative substitution factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{\\ln 2}^{\\ln 4}\\frac{6e^{x+1}}{e^{3x}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=-3\\int_{1-2\\ln 2}^{1-2\\ln 4}e^u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=-3\\left[e^u\\right]_{1-2\\ln 2}^{1-2\\ln 4} \\\\\n&=-3\\left(e^{1-2\\ln 4}-e^{1-2\\ln 2}\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $a>0$, $e^{1-2\\ln a}=e\\,a^{-2}=e/a^2$. Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3\\left(\\frac{e}{16}-\\frac{e}{4}\\right)\n&=-3\\left(-\\frac{3e}{16}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\frac{9e}{16}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe positive result agrees with the positive integrand and increasing original limits."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701908 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6617466-0188-518d-867b-0a1b32fcac60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6(e-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6617466-0188-518d-867b-0a1b32fcac60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6(e-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701907} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fc79c31-54a4-583a-b28b-b2d7c42c3369" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f66cdf2a-52b9-52fe-9284-20b322773077" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_0^2 3e^{x/2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=x/2$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2},\n\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=2\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nTransform both limits:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nNow evaluate in $u$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_0^2 3e^{x/2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=\\int_0^1 3e^u\\cdot 2\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=6\\int_0^1 e^u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=6\\left[e^u\\right]_0^1 \\\\\n&=6(e^1-e^0) \\\\\n&=6(e-1).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702076 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "353fe386-30a9-5fbd-90b8-846d0b2f5887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,e^{\\frac{x}{2} + 1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702078} {:answer/id #uuid "8db38ed7-41e6-5c40-b9cb-0cb07a6da2b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,e^{\\frac{x}{2} + 1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702094} {:answer/id #uuid "be22f555-a996-51f7-b619-aa47bf9020c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\,e^{\\frac{x}{2} + 1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702099} {:answer/id #uuid "e041696f-679e-58ab-abd7-fe74a8669e65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\,e^{\\frac{x}{2} + 1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702102} {:answer/id #uuid "efcc23cd-95cd-5bb2-8766-74c0635668fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\,e^{\\frac{x}{2} + 1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "353fe386-30a9-5fbd-90b8-846d0b2f5887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,e^{\\frac{x}{2} + 1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702078} :answer-field/id #uuid "598b02c3-6d87-5ff1-bedc-8dba968ee2f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2e9348a7-b85b-5303-96c2-1873ed3d96ee" :question/problem "Calculate the following integral.\n\n$$\n\\int 6\\,e^{\\frac{x}{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{x}{2} + 1$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=2\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nSubstitute, integrate, and replace $u$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int 6\\,e^{\\frac{x}{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int 6\\,e^{u}\\cdot\\left(2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&= 12\\,\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&= 12\\,e^{u}+C \\\\\n&= 12\\,e^{\\frac{x}{2} + 1}+C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the result gives $12\\,\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\,e^{\\frac{x}{2} + 1}=6\\,e^{\\frac{x}{2} + 1}$, as required."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702082 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cee47a5-bce9-58f9-b3ed-a284cff15fc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\,e^{2 - 2 x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702072} {:answer/id #uuid "23fee6cf-64c9-518e-9587-2b304af725a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,e^{2 - 2 x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702074} {:answer/id #uuid "6130d8b4-3463-5e9f-8aa8-e8022ab5e5de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\,e^{2 - 2 x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702086} {:answer/id #uuid "71a3caa4-8c02-508a-a332-dd1f47f4392f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\,e^{2 - 2 x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702089} {:answer/id #uuid "ef45b579-7288-5ac7-b78e-c75b532c247c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{12}\\,e^{2 - 2 x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71a3caa4-8c02-508a-a332-dd1f47f4392f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\,e^{2 - 2 x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702089} :answer-field/id #uuid "784e1ca1-6482-58b8-9b5a-cd5507c9282b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702090}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "57197659-17a5-5ed6-9e3e-179173e5728b" :question/problem "Calculate the following integral.\n\n$$\n\\int 6\\,e^{2 - 2 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2 - 2 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-2,\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=- \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nSubstitute, integrate, and replace $u$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int 6\\,e^{2 - 2 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int 6\\,e^{u}\\cdot\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&= -3\\,\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&= -3\\,e^{u}+C \\\\\n&= -3\\,e^{2 - 2 x}+C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the result gives $-3\\,\\left(-2\\right)\\,e^{2 - 2 x}=6\\,e^{2 - 2 x}$, as required."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702087 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "539cbf1a-2ed3-5f03-a6f4-f5c0274d8bb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,e^{2 x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702080} {:answer/id #uuid "553c9eb2-86fe-5d46-a62d-ad5d0e6ad9e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{4}\\,e^{2 x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702081} {:answer/id #uuid "b52b5f8e-e201-53b5-bdf3-244dc50ff2a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2}\\,e^{2 x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702098} {:answer/id #uuid "d3aadb79-fc63-51ae-a973-fa921dda0b40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\,e^{2 x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702100} {:answer/id #uuid "e98cf3de-ddff-5478-b7a5-79f6186c6c46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-e^{2 x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b52b5f8e-e201-53b5-bdf3-244dc50ff2a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2}\\,e^{2 x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702098} :answer-field/id #uuid "87737c44-62c9-5e4d-aba8-bc0a6cece238" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "642259fd-d1e5-5e54-8a05-216c7bd89376" :question/problem "Calculate the following integral.\n\n$$\n\\int -e^{2 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2,\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nSubstitute, integrate, and replace $u$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int -e^{2 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int -e^{u}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&= - \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&= - \\frac{1}{2}\\,e^{u}+C \\\\\n&= - \\frac{1}{2}\\,e^{2 x}+C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the result gives $- \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\left(2\\right)\\,e^{2 x}=-e^{2 x}$, as required."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702097 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3248eab6-179a-529e-a1b6-0222e6cc541d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\,e^{- \\frac{x}{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702077} {:answer/id #uuid "3653b86a-9dbb-5e7d-82fc-ddf18909fb01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\,e^{- \\frac{x}{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702079} {:answer/id #uuid "6c37e327-7121-599d-9035-c9799684ee53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}\\,e^{- \\frac{x}{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702088} {:answer/id #uuid "8cd838d1-1c6f-5da2-8d54-dfc3483e74b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,e^{- \\frac{x}{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702093} {:answer/id #uuid "90ad1a1d-ec61-54a5-bb73-d8bca38901ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}\\,e^{- \\frac{x}{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8cd838d1-1c6f-5da2-8d54-dfc3483e74b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,e^{- \\frac{x}{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702093} :answer-field/id #uuid "60f0d5ef-79ee-5b01-8bfb-fb2dd62818f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702085}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b19577a9-afc9-580a-8509-e5b1a0c3ccd1" :question/problem "Calculate the following integral.\n\n$$\n\\int -4\\,e^{- \\frac{x}{3}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=- \\frac{x}{3}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- \\frac{1}{3},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=-3\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nSubstitute, integrate, and replace $u$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int -4\\,e^{- \\frac{x}{3}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int -4\\,e^{u}\\cdot\\left(-3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&= 12\\,\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&= 12\\,e^{u}+C \\\\\n&= 12\\,e^{- \\frac{x}{3}}+C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the result gives $12\\,\\left(- \\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\,e^{- \\frac{x}{3}}=-4\\,e^{- \\frac{x}{3}}$, as required."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702101 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "264b9557-832f-5816-9cdc-08a3512a56b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{3}\\,e^{- 3 x - 1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702075} {:answer/id #uuid "5e2c3520-0c7c-5c8b-8d2f-b3ad61308551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,e^{- 3 x - 1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702084} {:answer/id #uuid "891dfbf6-b2f4-58ff-8bfd-9e5e91f91f3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,e^{- 3 x - 1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702092} {:answer/id #uuid "9a64ebfd-3570-5f7