}^{15}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Use $C$ for the arbitrary constant of integration.\n\n{{antiderivative}}" :question/worked-solution "Apply the power rule with $n=15$ and include an arbitrary constant $C$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x^{15}\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=\\frac{x^{15+1}}{15+1}+C \\\\ &=\\frac{x^{16}}{16}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCheck by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{x^{16}}{16}+C\\right)&=\\frac{1}{16}\\cdot 16x^{15}+0 \\\\ &=x^{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186704835 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a1627df-e486-501b-a8f0-4a9e394dc74e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{20}}{20}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a1627df-e486-501b-a8f0-4a9e394dc74e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{20}}{20}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704832} :answer-field/id #uuid "456088ff-55fa-5e43-b60a-c99ef8a22e5a" :answer-field/key "antiderivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704830}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d00eb424-29f8-51c1-83a9-f9d0e59fbee0" :question/problem "Calculate $F(x)$ given that $f(x)={x}^{19}$ and ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x).$ Use $C$ for the arbitrary constant of integration.\n\n$F(x)=$ {{antiderivative}}" :question/worked-solution "Integration reverses differentiation, so $F'(x)=f(x)$ gives $F(x)=\\int f(x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nApply the power rule with $n=19$ and include an arbitrary constant $C$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x)&=\\int x^{19}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\frac{x^{19+1}}{19+1}+C \\\\ &=\\frac{x^{20}}{20}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCheck by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{x^{20}}{20}+C\\right)&=\\frac{1}{20}\\cdot 20x^{19}+0 \\\\ &=x^{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186704837 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8810d54-d9e5-5b7c-883c-1fd4e263c50c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8810d54-d9e5-5b7c-883c-1fd4e263c50c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704836} :answer-field/id #uuid "e766b1b7-9dae-567a-9120-fb22041ad40f" :answer-field/key "antiderivative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "df16da36-a902-5c17-9016-49db16dba219" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int {x}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Use $C$ for the arbitrary constant of integration.\n\n{{antiderivative}}" :question/worked-solution "Apply the power rule with $n=1$ and include an arbitrary constant $C$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=\\frac{x^{1+1}}{1+1}+C \\\\ &=\\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCheck by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C\\right)&=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2x+0 \\\\ &=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705331 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d004b7a-9100-5ba1-b602-edc3c6da2355" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{16}{e^{2}} + \\frac{16}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d004b7a-9100-5ba1-b602-edc3c6da2355" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{16}{e^{2}} + \\frac{16}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705336} :answer-field/id #uuid "a915eafe-ba48-5d70-a6fd-247fe805ae55" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705339}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4bdadb75-847d-5c62-a4a4-15064eefed34" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-4}^{0} 4\\,e^{- 3 x - 1}\\,e^{\\frac{13 x}{4}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First apply the product rule for exponentials:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4\\,e^{- 3 x - 1}\\,e^{\\frac{13 x}{4}} &= 4\\,e^{(- 3 x - 1)+\\left(\\frac{13 x}{4}\\right)} \\\\\n&= 4\\,e^{\\frac{x}{4} - 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\frac{x}{4} - 1$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=4\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nTransform both limits, retaining their correspondence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|}\\hline x & -4 & 0 \\\\ \\hline u & -2 & -1 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nSubstitute and integrate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{-4}^{0} 4\\,e^{- 3 x - 1}\\,e^{\\frac{13 x}{4}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int_{-2}^{-1} 4\\,e^{u}\\cdot\\left(4\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&= 16\\,\\int_{-2}^{-1} e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&= 16\\,\\left[e^{u}\\right]_{-2}^{-1} \\\\\n&= 16\\,\\left(e^{-1}-e^{-2}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse $e^{-n}=1/e^n$ for negative exponents and $e^0=1$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ne^{-1} &= e^{-1} \\\\\ne^{-2} &= e^{-2} \\\\\n\\int_{-4}^{0} 4\\,e^{- 3 x - 1}\\,e^{\\frac{13 x}{4}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= 16\\,\\left((e^{-1})-(e^{-2})\\right) \\\\\n&= - \\frac{16}{e^{2}} + \\frac{16}{e}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705332 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "589fb129-b9c6-5359-b4ec-3955a4e79ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 e + 12 e^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "589fb129-b9c6-5359-b4ec-3955a4e79ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 e + 12 e^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705334} :answer-field/id #uuid "4df06e6a-6257-5481-8591-3b3c996da06f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4c37b2ac-cbf3-5c40-8da6-3043d5bcd2ba" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-3}^{3} \\frac{4\\,e^{2 - x}}{e^{- \\frac{4 x}{3}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First apply the quotient rule for exponentials:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{4\\,e^{2 - x}}{e^{- \\frac{4 x}{3}}} &= 4\\,e^{(2 - x)-\\left(- \\frac{4 x}{3}\\right)} \\\\\n&= 4\\,e^{\\frac{x}{3} + 2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\frac{x}{3} + 2$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=3\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nTransform both limits, retaining their correspondence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|}\\hline x & -3 & 3 \\\\ \\hline u & 1 & 3 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nSubstitute and integrate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{-3}^{3} \\frac{4\\,e^{2 - x}}{e^{- \\frac{4 x}{3}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int_{1}^{3} 4\\,e^{u}\\cdot\\left(3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&= 12\\,\\int_{1}^{3} e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&= 12\\,\\left[e^{u}\\right]_{1}^{3} \\\\\n&= 12\\,\\left(e^{3}-e^{1}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the exponentials at both endpoints, using $e^0=1$ when needed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ne^{3} &= e^{3} \\\\\ne^{1} &= e \\\\\n\\int_{-3}^{3} \\frac{4\\,e^{2 - x}}{e^{- \\frac{4 x}{3}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= 12\\,\\left((e^{3})-(e)\\right) \\\\\n&= - 12 e + 12 e^{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705335 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98b1a827-d122-58b7-8453-ed2b2809f618" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 e^{3} + 6 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98b1a827-d122-58b7-8453-ed2b2809f618" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 e^{3} + 6 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705338} :answer-field/id #uuid "07dae219-7f03-5662-b27f-669313211d69" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "741ad30c-113d-53e3-957d-fa7d5f497951" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-2}^{2} -3\\,e^{x + 2}\\,e^{- \\frac{3 x}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First apply the product rule for exponentials:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3\\,e^{x + 2}\\,e^{- \\frac{3 x}{2}} &= -3\\,e^{(x + 2)+\\left(- \\frac{3 x}{2}\\right)} \\\\\n&= -3\\,e^{2 - \\frac{x}{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=2 - \\frac{x}{2}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- \\frac{1}{2},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=-2\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nTransform both limits, retaining their correspondence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|}\\hline x & -2 & 2 \\\\ \\hline u & 3 & 1 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nThe transformed limits decrease. Keep this order together with the negative differential factor.\n\nSubstitute and integrate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{-2}^{2} -3\\,e^{x + 2}\\,e^{- \\frac{3 x}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int_{3}^{1} -3\\,e^{u}\\cdot\\left(-2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&= 6\\,\\int_{3}^{1} e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&= 6\\,\\left[e^{u}\\right]_{3}^{1} \\\\\n&= 6\\,\\left(e^{1}-e^{3}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the exponentials at both endpoints, using $e^0=1$ when needed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ne^{1} &= e \\\\\ne^{3} &= e^{3} \\\\\n\\int_{-2}^{2} -3\\,e^{x + 2}\\,e^{- \\frac{3 x}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= 6\\,\\left((e)-(e^{3})\\right) \\\\\n&= - 6 e^{3} + 6 e\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705340 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8af1aa5-fc04-57b5-b621-d364fc175686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{7}{3 e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8af1aa5-fc04-57b5-b621-d364fc175686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{7}{3 e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705341} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f01b8f9-6a3c-58e4-83f9-fba86268fa34" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705337}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e189e830-96b9-5c43-8628-ef77bb04dd4e" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\ln{(2 )}} -e^{2 x - 1}\\,e^{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First apply the product rule for exponentials:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-e^{2 x - 1}\\,e^{x} &= -e^{(2 x - 1)+(x)} \\\\\n&= -e^{3 x - 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=3 x - 1$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=3,\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nTransform both limits, retaining their correspondence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|}\\hline x & 0 & \\ln{(2 )} \\\\ \\hline u & -1 & -1 + 3 \\ln{(2 )} \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nSubstitute and integrate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{\\ln{(2 )}} -e^{2 x - 1}\\,e^{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int_{-1}^{-1 + 3 \\ln{(2 )}} -e^{u}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&= - \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\int_{-1}^{-1 + 3 \\ln{(2 )}} e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&= - \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\left[e^{u}\\right]_{-1}^{-1 + 3 \\ln{(2 )}} \\\\\n&= - \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\left(e^{-1 + 3 \\ln{(2 )}}-e^{-1}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $t>0$, use $e^{b+k\\ln t}=e^b t^k$. A negative power satisfies $t^{-n}=1/t^n$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ne^{-1 + 3 \\ln{(2 )}} &= \\frac{8}{e} \\\\\ne^{-1} &= e^{-1} \\\\\n\\int_{0}^{\\ln{(2 )}} -e^{2 x - 1}\\,e^{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= - \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\left(\\left(\\frac{8}{e}\\right)-(e^{-1})\\right) \\\\\n&= - \\frac{7}{3 e}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705454 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "682ba48e-233a-560b-bcb6-b3fbd9ee593f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{16\\ln 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705456}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "682ba48e-233a-560b-bcb6-b3fbd9ee593f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{16\\ln 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705456} :answer-field/id #uuid "c66f4058-b29a-5a9b-9610-9a7875b84d2c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705459}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1c0c86fa-5a49-5d78-93e6-6e4f03245231" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^{1} \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{2x+1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2x+1$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nTransform both limits, keeping their corresponding order:\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-1$ | $3$ |\n\nUse the logarithm quotient law:\n\n$$\n\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=\\ln 1-\\ln 2=-\\ln 2.\n$$\n\nNow integrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{-1}^{1} \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{2x+1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=\\frac{\\int_{-1}^{3} \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u}{2} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\left[\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{u}}{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}\\right]_{-1}^{3}}{2} \\\\ &=-\\frac{1}{2\\ln 2}\\left[\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{u}\\right]_{-1}^{3} \\\\ &=-\\frac{1}{2\\ln 2}\\left(\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{3}-\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{-1}\\right) \\\\ &=-\\frac{1}{2\\ln 2}\\left(\\frac{1}{8}-2\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{15}{16\\ln 2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe answer is positive because the integrand is positive and the original limits increase."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705457 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "deda6d97-51a9-5433-b21e-bb79cd76228f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2\\ln 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "deda6d97-51a9-5433-b21e-bb79cd76228f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2\\ln 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705463} :answer-field/id #uuid "fde102b2-5dbf-5539-a54f-daf41db21d60" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8966ea68-b907-5c7c-b0d1-3a94460cebc4" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^{0} \\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)^{-2x-2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=-2x-2$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\mathrm{d}x=- \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nTransform both limits, keeping their corresponding order:\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $-2$ |\n\nUse the logarithm quotient law:\n\n$$\n\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)=\\ln 1-\\ln 4=-\\ln 4.\n$$\n\nNow integrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{-1}^{0} \\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)^{-2x-2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=-\\frac{\\int_{0}^{-2} \\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u}{2} \\\\ &=-\\frac{\\left[\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)^{u}}{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)}\\right]_{0}^{-2}}{2} \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2\\ln 4}\\left[\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)^{u}\\right]_{0}^{-2} \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2\\ln 4}\\left(\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)^{-2}-\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)^{0}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2\\ln 4}\\left(16-1\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{15}{2\\ln 4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe answer is positive because the integrand is positive and the original limits increase."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705458 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "224cfaad-45a6-5a80-ad63-5fbaa300273f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9\\ln 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "224cfaad-45a6-5a80-ad63-5fbaa300273f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9\\ln 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705455} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7e68dfd-3349-5162-bbf5-afbeb2a9edc8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ac915b67-0672-5ef0-a1f1-07379ce376d0" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{2} 3\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^{2x-1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2x-1$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nTransform both limits, keeping their corresponding order:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n\nUse the logarithm quotient law:\n\n$$\n\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)=\\ln 1-\\ln 3=-\\ln 3.\n$$\n\nNow integrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{1}^{2} 3\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^{2x-1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=\\frac{3\\cdot \\int_{1}^{3} \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u}{2} \\\\ &=\\frac{3\\cdot \\left[\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^{u}}{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}\\right]_{1}^{3}}{2} \\\\ &=-\\frac{3}{2\\ln 3}\\left[\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^{u}\\right]_{1}^{3} \\\\ &=-\\frac{3}{2\\ln 3}\\left(\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^{3}-\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^{1}\\right) \\\\ &=-\\frac{3}{2\\ln 3}\\left(\\frac{1}{27}-\\frac{1}{3}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{4}{9\\ln 3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe answer is positive because the integrand is positive and the original limits increase."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705461 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de892e86-5ea0-5075-9c00-912c6ae524a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\ln 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de892e86-5ea0-5075-9c00-912c6ae524a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\ln 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705462} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b49d9d7-30a8-5fa5-8bdb-00265758b7fa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ccc0b5a2-cdab-5d51-87bc-72b372d1166f" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^{0} 2\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{-x+1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=-x+1$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\mathrm{d}x=-1\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nTransform both limits, keeping their corresponding order:\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $1$ |\n\nUse the logarithm quotient law:\n\n$$\n\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=\\ln 1-\\ln 2=-\\ln 2.\n$$\n\nNow integrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{-1}^{0} 2\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{-x+1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x&=-2\\cdot \\int_{2}^{1} \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ &=-2\\cdot \\left[\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{u}}{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}\\right]_{2}^{1} \\\\ &=\\frac{2}{\\ln 2}\\left[\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{u}\\right]_{2}^{1} \\\\ &=\\frac{2}{\\ln 2}\\left(\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{1}-\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{2}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{2}{\\ln 2}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2\\ln 2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe answer is positive because the integrand is positive and the original limits increase."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716935 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32e312ef-38df-55d0-a292-8e586a713fea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32e312ef-38df-55d0-a292-8e586a713fea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716940} :answer-field/id #uuid "34876873-0a72-5506-82ba-acbbebe653ca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716943}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "01ca9f59-062c-5d62-a4a1-5d091bddc512" :question/problem "Calculate $\\det(C)$, given that\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n$\\det(C)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, multiply the main diagonal entries and subtract the product of the off-diagonal entries:\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nEach diagonal contains two negative entries, so both products are positive. Keep the order: main-diagonal product minus off-diagonal product.\n\nThe determinant can be negative; determinant bars do not mean absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det(C) &=(-2)(-5)-(-3)(-4) \\\\ &=10-12 \\\\ &=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716938 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03caa3a5-ae8d-5f2b-9f48-fb424e738839" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716936} {:answer/id #uuid "05b10cba-f8c9-5089-a296-0732e8cb9e54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716937} {:answer/id #uuid "32f75a31-4b5c-5237-bde4-f27a2e1f5a17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716941} {:answer/id #uuid "335df867-4021-5b0b-bb1e-478d114bed8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716942} {:answer/id #uuid "b40a3b19-da66-5ead-8bcf-931fec634843" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716948}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32f75a31-4b5c-5237-bde4-f27a2e1f5a17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716941} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c23926e-5529-5d15-8af8-3d8b3e772218" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716944}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0aa10523-be4a-57fe-9858-f98da39469b6" :question/problem "Calculate $\\det(A)$, given that\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, multiply the main diagonal entries and subtract the product of the off-diagonal entries:\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\n![The blue main diagonal gives ad; subtract bc from the red off-diagonal. ](images/25/2594f99e0f02241dc6d01f85c82923103df1d6fb4dda5ca03d438637f5178a28.png)\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det(A) &=(2)(4)-(1)(3) \\\\ &=8-3 \\\\ &=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716945 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94466079-59c9-574e-a114-ce7e2fd929a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716946} {:answer/id #uuid "94e4532c-f041-5571-b77b-826e17dce420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716947} {:answer/id #uuid "bfa7b27b-2a84-5cc3-840e-06bf1d8a9950" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716949} {:answer/id #uuid "d9430131-9b2d-50d8-a884-36c769943088" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716950} {:answer/id #uuid "ea5ea099-f7c9-573c-9426-c7b32f0c040e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea5ea099-f7c9-573c-9426-c7b32f0c040e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716951} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ccb7a7d-cec7-57f9-b016-76cbedd45391" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716939}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "58f6ea98-a4e7-583f-b58c-838a38934da5" :question/problem "Calculate $\\det(B)$, given that\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, multiply the main diagonal entries and subtract the product of the off-diagonal entries:\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nThe off-diagonal product is negative: $(3)(-4)=-12$. Subtracting this negative product adds $12$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det(B) &=(2)(1)-(3)(-4) \\\\ &=2-(-12) \\\\ &=2+12 \\\\ &=14.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720756 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04713f39-9754-5ff6-a14b-f6e2cd7a7d30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\cos y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720753} {:answer/id #uuid "128a0c08-ea82-5b34-9a89-c143ac729914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\cos y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720754} {:answer/id #uuid "7ef054b6-9ffc-5602-8ade-80666635b17f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}\\sin y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720758} {:answer/id #uuid "ada34dfa-7d3d-55e5-b373-0261655d5110" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sin y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720763} {:answer/id #uuid "c743cd6a-c909-5ae5-ba0b-2fdfacc6b9cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sin y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c743cd6a-c909-5ae5-ba0b-2fdfacc6b9cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sin y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720766} :answer-field/id #uuid "bccc3932-5432-545d-ae41-ac6277ef06bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720765}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5ce02a7d-904a-54ae-827c-bc7a88000c4c" :question/problem "Calculate\n\n$$\n\\int (-3\\cos y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\cos y\\,\\mathrm{d}y=\\sin y+C.\n$$\n\nTake the constant factor outside the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int (-3\\cos y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n&=-3\\int \\cos y\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\\n&=-3\\sin y+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $-3\\sin y+C$ is $-3\\cos y$, as required."}]}
